Article 2 (Criteria for Designation of Traditional Martial Arts Eligible for Fostering) The criteria for designating traditional martial arts eligible for fostering under Article 6 (1) of the Promotion of Traditional Martial Arts Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") shall be as follows:
1. It shall be possible to substantiate the fact of their transmission through literature, records, oral traditions, or other materials;
2. Their technical systems, weapons, dress, training systems, etiquette, and terminology shall reflect the traditional characteristics of the Republic of Korea;
3. They shall contribute to the dissemination of cultural values, including by carrying out transmission activities with facilities, personnel, and programs;
4. They shall have an established technical system and training system;
5. They shall have value as a sport, including the enhancement of physical fitness and the cultivation of character.
